      { prompt: "Which piece fits in this hole?", say: "Which piece fits in this hole?" },
      { prompt: "Which one is the cat's shadow?", say: "Which one is the cat's shadow?" },
      { prompt: "Whose shadow is this?", say: "Whose shadow is this?" },
      { prompt: "Match each piece to its own hole", say: "Match each piece to its own hole" },
      { text: "The shadow game: in the evening, use a torch or a phone light to cast the shadows of a few things on the wall (a glass, a spoon, a doll, your hand) and let your child guess what they are. Then play “What's missing?”: draw a face or a house and leave one thing out (the mouth, the door, the chimney) for your child to find. If you have a jigsaw, take out one piece and ask which piece fills the gap. Ask: “How did you know?”" }
